erence Between Afternoon Tea and High Tea?","target":"https://www.thespruceeats.com/afternoon-vs-high-tea-difference-435327","line":50},{"title":"French Onion Soup – Recipe, History & Where to Eat it in Paris","target":"https://worldinparis.com/french-onion-soup","line":52},{"title":"Breakfast, lunch and dinner: Have we always eaten them","target":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/magazine-20243692","line":56},{"title":"▲","target":"https://www.tastesofhistory.co.uk/post/#viewer-lor1i176","line":56},{"title":"▲","target":"https://www.tastesofhistory.co.uk/post/#viewer-7nfur196","line":58}],"metadata":{"title":"A Brief History of Food: The evolution of mealtimes","source":"https://www.tastesofhistory.co.uk/post/a-brief-history-of-food-the-evolution-of-mealtimes","author":null,"published":"2025-02-26","created":"2025-04-28","description":"What follows was inspired by the video “Vegetables don’t exist” on the “Words Unravelled!” YouTube channel hosted by Rob Watts from “RobWords” and Jess Zafarris author of the etymology books “Words from Hell” and “Once Upon a Word”.Meal Times  As Tastes Of History is based in the UK our focus on food history and recipes is unashamedly British and Euro-centric. Clearly, however, cuisine and dining in the “Old World” has been heavily influenced by pretty much all areas of the globe. Putting aside","tags":[]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"pphupc","at":1778088457429},"key":"Clippings/A Brief History of Food The evolution of mealtimes.md"},
